        "original_id": "2b45cde8-7d87-5db6-9a68-5be8eaafa188",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tie Domi, Bill Watters, Paul Beeston, Bobby Orr, Max Domi\n- Organizations: Maple Leaf Sports & Entertainment, Toronto Maple Leafs, Toronto Blue Jays\n- Teams: Ontario Raiders, Toronto Rock\n- Places: Toronto, Maple Leaf Gardens\n- Topics: team ownership, relocation, rebranding, biography, family relationships\n\nFacts:\n- Tie Domi was born on November 1, 1969, and he is a retired Canadian professional ice hockey player of Albanian origin.\n- A group including Bill Watters, Paul Beeston, Tie Domi, and Bobby Orr bought the Ontario Raiders for $250,000 after Maple Leaf Sports & Entertainment considered purchasing the team.\n- The new ownership group promptly relocated the Ontario Raiders to Toronto's Maple Leaf Gardens and rebranded the team as the Toronto Rock.\n- Bill Watters was the Assistant General Manager of the Toronto Maple Leafs at the time of the Ontario Raiders purchase.\n- Paul Beeston was the former president of the Toronto Blue Jays at the time of the Ontario Raiders purchase.\n- Tie Domi was a player for the Toronto Maple Leafs at the time of the Ontario Raiders purchase.\n- Bobby Orr was a former NHL player at the time of the Ontario Raiders purchase.\n- Max Domi's father is former Toronto Maple Leafs player Tie Domi.",
